# S3b: the TP4 G1 reference for S3a: the same matrix plan and the same four real-text prompts (the image builds them from its own
# corpus by length) on general-tp4 (the general path: no fast path, the device sampler), 256 tokens out (its output ceiling). Its
# solo texts are what S3a's solo texts are compared with, offline, per user: where the first divergence falls. Bit equality is
# not expected (another engine and another reduction order); a first divergence at a near-tie after a long agreeing prefix is the
# pass reading. SOFT: a verdict other than PASS here does not stop the window, the texts are the product. Run after S3a's arms
# completed.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card S2 window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/s2 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here
# names a rig, a card or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. A placeholder in @...@ is filled in by whoever drives
# the window (the graft directory and the graft binary digest of the one-card harnesses); every other value is final.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image S0 builds from this same commit; a later commit needs a new tag.
# Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min; per arm an engine build 3-8 min plus 3-8 min of streams; two arms 15-35 min.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset gate
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-s2-1
C2_PROFILE=general-tp4
C2_GATE_PLAN=matrix
C2_GATE_LENGTHS=4096,16384,32768,60000
C2_GATE_MAX_TOKENS=256
